Content area from OpenRune/OpenRune-Server#353 (answers there: all of it, one PR per row, ids renumbered against main, wiki data is fine).

From our per-feature patches `12-quests-sheep-shearer-romeo-juliet`, `67-vampyre-slayer` (in [`openrune/upstream/`](https://github.com/AlexPerrin/osrs-plugins-reverse/tree/main/openrune/upstream) of osrs-plugins-reverse), on `main` (`1be5dfb5f`).

Stacked on the Sheep Shearer / Romeo & Juliet PR (its `QuestTalkFixture`); only the last commit is new here. Merged after that PR, this one shows only its own commit.

**Problem.** Vampyre Slayer was not implemented. Morgan always gave his after-quest lines (the Draynor script asked "completed?", which the default assume-completed quest mode always answers with yes), and the Blue Moon Inn had no bartender, so the quest's beer step could not be done.

**Change.** New quest on the OSRS progress varp 178 (`varp.vampire`) through the server-only varbit `vampyre_slayer_progress`: 0, 1 started, 2 stake received, 3 complete (the cache dbrow end state, checked at startup). These are the values Quest Helper keys its steps on.
- Morgan and Dr Harlow: start, legends, garlic hint, Harlow's beer, stake, topics, a lost stake; Harlow's client varbits `harlow_given_beer` / `harlow_given_stake` are set. Morgan's garlic cupboard opens and gives garlic.
- Opening the coffin in the manor basement at stages 1-2 raises Count Draynor for that player (500-tick lifespan, removed on logout). Garlic in the inventory weakens him (-10 hitpoints, -10 Attack/Strength, -40 Defence). At 0 hitpoints a stake and a hammer finish him (quest complete: 3 QP, 4,825 Attack XP); otherwise he regenerates to full.
- Morgan's after-quest dialogue moves from `DraynorVillageNpcs` into the quest.
- New `BlueMoonBartender`: "A glass of your finest ale please." sells a beer for 2 coins, plus the fortune and equipment topics.

Server-only ids, numbered after the ids already on main and not shared with any of our other PRs, so they merge in any order: varp `vampyre_slayer_state` 63713; varbits `vampyre_slayer_progress` 63720, `vampyre_asked_harlow` 63721.

**Tests.** `VampyreSlayerInteractionTest` (5): start, decline, Harlow's beer before the stake, a lost stake replaced, Morgan's garlic hint; plus the suites it builds on. Manual, on our own server build: a full run with Quest Helper 4.18 on the RuneLite desktop client (fresh account): every step showed the right QH text, varp 178 went 0-1-2-3, the bartender's beer turned QH's requirement green, and the kill completed the quest.

On this branch (Docker `eclipse-temurin:21`, upstream's `./gradlew`, 4 GB container; a clean `freshCache` of main restored first, then `:or-cache:buildCache :or-cache:mergePluginGamevals`, then each task as a separate run, then `run` to "Server ready"): RESULTS_PENDING. `tools/scripts/fix_gameval_conflicts.py --check` finds no conflicts on this branch, nor with all of our open content PRs merged together.

Nothing was checked in game from this exact branch; the in-game checks above were on our own server build (an older main plus these and our other patches).

**Data sources.** OSRS Wiki (by the wiki's contributors, CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/): dialogue from the wiki transcripts (Morgan, Dr Harlow, Bartender (Blue Moon Inn), Vampyre Slayer); rewards, garlic effects and locations from the quest page. Step values: Quest Helper's `VampyreSlayer` (BSD) and the cache dbrow `quest_vampyreslayer`.

**Caveats.**
- Guesses: the cupboard's take message, "The coffin is sealed shut." outside the quest, the Count's attack animation, keeping the stake after the kill.
- Simplified: the garlic weakening lasts until he respawns (the wiki ties it to the first melee hit and 30 seconds); his fast regeneration and return to the coffin are not implemented.

**Release note.** Vampyre Slayer is playable; the Blue Moon Inn has its bartender.

